olimits(F)$, the group of automorphisms of the given $\mathbb{G}$-structure $F$ on $S-(M\cap S^\circ)$. This group was described in Proposition ef {prop:G-structures} (a1)(b1), in particular it is abelian. Further, $\phi\in\operatorname{Diff}(S,M)$ lies in $\operatorname{Im}(\pi)$ if and only if the $\mathbb{G}$-structure $\phi^*F$ on $S-(M\cap S^\circ)$ is isomorphic to $F$. So $\operatorname{Im}(\pi)$ is the stabilizer of the action of $\operatorname{Diff}(S,M)$ on the set of isomorphism classes of objects of $\mathbb{G}\operatorname{Str}(S-(M\cap S^\circ))$. This set was described in Proposition ef {prop:G-structures} (a2)(b2), in particular, it is discrete. So $\operatorname{Im}(\pi)$ is open and closed, and similarly for $\operatorname{Im}(\pi_{\operatorname{pure}})$.

